WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.045 --> 00:00:06.590 position:66% line:0%
I'm Ryan O'Connell, the writer and creator
of the new Netflix series,<i> Special.</i>

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.218 line:0%
And with me today
is the star of<i> Special...</i>

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.053 line:0%
Ryan O'Connell!

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:12.763 line:0%
Thank you for having me.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.973 line:0%
Am I backlit?

00:00:15.307 --> 00:00:16.141 line:0%
You're fine.

00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:19.353 line:0%
So,<i> Special</i> is based on
our shared life experiences.

00:00:19.436 --> 00:00:22.689 position:66% line:0%
Not to be a bitch,
but it's actually more my life experience,

00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:26.985 line:0%
because I'm the one who had to
live it out on screen, fearlessly.

00:00:27.069 --> 00:00:31.657 line:0%
But if you didn't have my words
you would have nothing to live out.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.284 line:0%
I hear you, but I also don't.

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:39.540 line:0%
OK, well, what makes<i> Special</i> so...
special...

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:44.086 line:0%
is that it takes someone who's been
kind of othered in our society,

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:47.548 line:0%
and through brilliant,
thought-provoking writing,

00:00:47.631 --> 00:00:48.924 line:0%
it normalizes him.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:52.469 line:0%
I really think it was my acting
that helped normalize this.

00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:55.848 position:61% line:0%
When I first got the script for<i> Special</i>
it was under a pile of scripts

00:00:55.931 --> 00:00:57.516 line:0%
because I get so many offers.

00:00:57.599 --> 00:01:01.478 position:56% line:0%
And I got the script finally,
and I loved it, but I also wondered,

00:01:01.562 --> 00:01:06.608 line:0%
"Where does Ryan end
and the real Ryan begin?"

00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:09.653 position:58% line:0%
Yeah, that should've been really easy
because he's literally you, so...

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.822 position:61% line:0%
That's not what my acting teacher said.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.532 line:0%
I slaved over these scripts,

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:18.036 line:0%
these beautiful, gorgeous,
stunning, thought-provoking scripts

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.371 line:0%
for two years.

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:21.623 position:61% line:0%
Does writing not come naturally to you?

00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:23.000 line:0%
It's funny that you say that,

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.502 line:0%
because actually it
poured out of me like a geyser.

00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:27.880 line:0%
Like, I literally needed, like,
a clean-up on, like, aisle four

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:29.006 line:0%
because I was just gushing.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.925 line:0%
It's writing, it's a craft,
it's not like acting, no offense.

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:34.595 line:0%
I think that the quality
really shows in the writing.

00:01:34.678 --> 00:01:35.721 line:0%
It's good because I'm good.

00:01:35.804 --> 00:01:38.849 position:61% line:0%
Just let everyone decide for themselves
when they see it, you know?

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:42.394 line:0%
Writing... acting.

00:01:44.146 --> 00:01:45.856 line:0%
They'll decide, they know.

